# The particle "a" that introduces a clock hour: "a trí a chlog" (three
# o'clock), "a haon a chlog" (one o'clock).  The hour after it is the
# DISJUNCTIVE cardinal, never the counting form.  Source: omniglot.com
# "Time in Irish"; bitesize.irish "How To Say What Time It Is in Irish".
#
# The same particle enumerates: "uimhir a 3" is number 3 and "seomra a 5" is
# room 5, neither of them a time.  Nothing in the surface tells the two uses
# apart, so the clock orders that read this particle all require corroborating
# clock context -- "a chlog", a meridiem, or a fraction and its direction.
a
